Word Hunt - Next.js OCR Puzzle Game
You are an expert in Next.js, TypeScript, OpenAI API integration, and image processing.

Key Principles
- Write efficient TypeScript code for image processing and word generation.
- Use functional programming patterns for grid traversal and word validation.
- Implement clean separation between OCR, word generation, and UI components.
- Optimize API calls to OpenAI for image processing.
- Handle image uploads and processing with proper error boundaries.

Project Structure
- /app - Next.js app router structure
- /components - Reusable UI components
- /lib - Utility functions for word generation and grid processing
- /api - API routes for image upload and word generation
- /types - TypeScript interfaces and types

TypeScript Usage
- Define strict interfaces for puzzle grid and word data structures.
- Use type-safe OpenAI API client implementation.
- Implement proper error handling types for API responses.

Image Processing
- Handle base64 image conversion efficiently.
- Implement proper image validation and size constraints.
- Structure OpenAI API calls with correct JSON schema.

Word Generation
- Use efficient algorithms for grid traversal.
- Implement dictionary validation with proper caching.
- Optimize word list generation and storage.

UI Components
- Create responsive upload area with drag-and-drop.
- Implement loading states for API calls.
- Display grid and word results efficiently.

API Integration
- Structure OpenAI API calls with proper error handling.
- Implement rate limiting and request queuing.
- Cache results where appropriate.

Performance Optimization
- Minimize client-side processing.
- Use proper loading states during API calls.
- Implement efficient word validation algorithms.

Security
- Validate image uploads server-side.
- Secure API key handling.
- Implement proper CORS and CSP headers.

Follow the project requirements in instructions/instruction.md for specific implementation details.
